## Project structure

```text
.
|-- .github/workflows/   # continuous integration{% if deployment != 'none' %} and deployment{% endif %}
|-- .vscode/             # recommended editor settings and tasks
|-- docs/                # architecture documentation
|-- public/              # assets copied without transformation
|-- src/
|   |-- app/             # composition, routing, shell, errors, and providers
|   |   |-- errors/      # application-level error handling
|   |   |-- layout/      # concrete application shell components
|   |   `-- providers/   # application-wide React contexts
|   |-- components/
|   |   |-- layout/      # generic layout primitives
|   |   `-- ui/          # generic presentational components
|   |-- features/        # documented extension point for product capabilities
|   |-- hooks/           # generic React hooks
|   |-- lib/             # framework-independent infrastructure
|   |   `-- api/         # HTTP boundary and API errors
|   |-- pages/           # route-level components
|   |-- styles/          # reset, design tokens, and global utilities
|   |-- test/            # shared component-test setup
|   `-- main.tsx         # browser entry point
{% if include_express %}|-- server/               # optional Express server and API
|   |-- config/          # validated server environment
|   |-- routes/          # infrastructure and API routes
|   |-- app.ts           # middleware and route composition
|   `-- index.ts         # process bootstrap and network listener
{% endif %}|-- tests/e2e/            # Playwright browser tests
|-- package.json         # dependencies and project commands
|-- tsconfig.json        # TypeScript project references
|-- typedoc.json         # API documentation configuration
`-- vite.config.ts       # development and production build
```
{% if include_express %}

The optional server separates application construction from process startup. `app.ts`
can be imported without opening a port, while `index.ts` owns only environment loading
and the network listener. Organize a larger backend by feature and compose its routers
in `app.ts` instead of adding unrelated logic to the bootstrap.
{% endif %}

See [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md) for dependency boundaries, extension
points, and examples.

